is_device_mounted() reads /etc/mtab and calls a device unmounted when that
file cannot be opened.  LikeOS has no /etc/mtab; the table of mounted file
systems is /proc/mounts, which is read when /etc/mtab is missing.  (The
O_EXCL open of the target stays the second line of defence: the kernel
refuses it with EBUSY while the device is mounted.)

